# PNGs are plain git blobs, not LFS objects.
#
# This file used to declare `*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs`, but
# nothing was ever committed through LFS — every image is stored as a real
# PNG. Once CI checked out with `lfs: true`, git configured the LFS clean
# filter, and `git diff` then rewrote each working-tree PNG to a pointer
# before comparing, so every image looked modified and the version lock
# failed on a branch that had touched no content.
#
# `-text` is kept: it is the half of the old line that was true, and it
# stops any end-of-line normalisation being applied to binary files.
*.png -text
